# TrendVaulta API — look up routes in the repo

Use this rule when wiring endpoints, verifying contracts, or reviewing API behavior. **Do not guess paths** — look them up in `apps/api/routes/` and the matching controller.

There is **no**  trendvaulta / API-3 extract in this repo. Do not search for `api_latest_extracted.txt`, `api3_endpoint_index.txt`, or `frontend/src/lib/.../endpoints.ts`.

## Files in this repo (sole sources)

| Location | Role |
|---|---|
| `apps/api/routes/` | Express route definitions + middleware |
| `apps/api/controllers/` | Business logic and response contracts |
| `apps/api/models/` | Mongoose schemas + Joi validators |
| `apps/api/app.js` | Route mounts, Stripe webhook, CORS |
| `apps/website/src/lib/api.ts` | Storefront HTTP client |
| `apps/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts` | Dashboard HTTP client |
| `packages/api-client/` | Shared client (used by dashboard) |

## Lookup workflow (token-efficient)

1. Search `apps/api/routes/` for the path/method.
2. Read only the matching controller section for auth, body/query, status codes, and response shape.
3. Check the model for field types and validation.
4. Mirror existing frontend patterns in `apps/website/src/hooks/` or `apps/dashboard/src/hooks/`.

## Path prefixes

- Backend mounts under `/api/` (see `app.js`).
- Storefront/dashboard call the API via their `api.ts` clients (and Vite proxy `/api` → `http://localhost:3000` on dashboard).
- Stripe webhook: `POST /api/webhooks/stripe` (raw body) in `app.js`.

## Response & error contract

- Prefer confirming per controller; common shape is `{ message, data?, errors? }` or direct payload + `message`.
- Auth: `Authorization: Bearer <token>` via `verfiyToken` (existing spelling).
- Validation: Joi in models/controllers — typically **400** with message/`errors`.
- Lists: check controller for `page` / `limit` / `total` / results array naming.
- User-facing copy: Arabic-first where helpers already exist — never show raw internal codes in UI.

## Integration checklist

- [ ] Route exists in `apps/api/routes/` and is mounted in `app.js`
- [ ] Controller auth role matches the screen (public / user / admin permissions)
- [ ] Request/response shape matches controller
- [ ] Storefront or dashboard client + React Query hook updated
- [ ] Loading and safe error UX match surrounding screens

## Key domain areas

| Area | Routes (examples) | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **Auth / profile** | `/api/auth/*`, `/api/profile`, `/api/password/*` | JWT login/register/reset |
| **Products** | `/api/products/*` | Catalog, badges, sort (e.g. bestselling) |
| **Brands** | `/api/brands/*` | Featured brands supported |
| **Orders** | `/api/orders/*` | Create, my orders, admin |
| **Payments** | `/api/payments/*`, webhook | Stripe checkout + paid marking |
| **Wishlist** | `/api/wishlist/*` | Auth user wishlist |
| **Reviews** | `/api/reviews/*` | User + admin review management |
| **Coupons / offers** | `/api/coupons/*`, `/api/offers/*` | Promotions |
| **Recommendations / bundles** | `/api/recommendations/*`, `/api/bundles/*` | Storefront rails |
| **Recently viewed** | `/api/recently-viewed` (confirm path in routes) | Sync browsing history |
| **Gift finder / lookbooks** | gift-finder, lookbooks routes | Discovery content |
| **Storefront content** | trust, categories, testimonials, why-choose-us | Homepage content APIs |
| **Admin stats** | `/api/admin/...` stats routes | Dashboard home metrics |
| **trendvaulta** | `/api/trendvaulta`, `/api/ready` when mounted | Ops / Render readiness |

## Domain traps

| Topic | Rule |
|---|---|
| **Not templates** | Catalog is **products/brands**, not digital templates/creators. |
| **Ports** | API **3000**, website **3001**, dashboard **3002**. |
| **Package manager** | **npm** workspaces — not pnpm. |
| **Demo fallbacks** | Storefront may fall back to `apps/website/src/data/demoStorefront.ts` when APIs fail; prefer live APIs when wiring new rails. |
| **Permissions** | Admin actions use role/permission helpers (e.g. `rolePermissions.js`) — check before adding admin CRUD. |
| **Stripe** | Paid side-effects (salesCount, confirmation email) live in payment/order paid flows — read those controllers before changing checkout. |
